    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe structure is clean and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- The repeated \"first three letters, upper-cased\" logic for city and last name is factored into a single `prefix(String)` helper rather than duplicated inline \u2014 the right call, and it also centralizes the null-handling.\n- Format logic stays entirely within `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.service`, the natural unit for it. No format knowledge leaks elsewhere.\n- I checked the one value derived from `customerCode` (`membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper`, line 26-28): it concatenates the whole `customerCode` string (`owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + ...`) rather than parsing its internal shape, so it rebuilds on the new format automatically with no structural change required. Nothing became stale, and no parsing/format duplication was introduced.\n- The Javadoc was updated to match the new format and example \u2014 consistent with the code.\n\nThe only nit is stylistic, not structural: `owner.getCity() != null` is re-evaluated inside the `filter` lambda for every element even though it's loop-invariant. That's an efficiency/readability micro-point, not a matter of logic living in the wrong place, so it doesn't warrant changes here.",
